# =============================================================================
# ALLOWLIST, not a denylist -- and that is deliberate.
#
# This directory is not a clean project root. It also holds the LEGACY .NET
# backend and React frontends (Backend/, CoreLibraries/, DataModel/,
# FinCoreMainNew/, Frontend/, Fin_Connect_Cms_React/, ib-admin-portal-ui/,
# New_fin/, AML-*/). That code is reference material for understanding the
# business domain. It is proprietary and this repository is PUBLIC, so it must
# never be committed.
#
# A denylist ("ignore node_modules, ignore .env") fails open: anything nobody
# thought of gets committed. An allowlist fails closed: anything nobody thought
# of is ignored. For a public repo sharing a parent directory with proprietary
# source, fail-closed is the only defensible choice.
#
# Verify with `git ls-files` before every first push, not with hope.
# =============================================================================

# Ignore every top-level entry ...
/*

# ... then re-admit only what belongs to THIS project.
!/.gitignore
!/.github/
!/ledgercore/
!/ledgercore-web/
!/README.md

# Phase write-ups for the NEW system.
!/PHASE2_ARCHITECTURE.md
!/PHASE3_BACKEND_FOUNDATION.md
!/PHASE4_AUTHENTICATION.md
!/PHASE5_LEDGER.md
!/PHASE6_REDIS.md
!/PHASE7_ASYNC.md
!/PHASE8_LOAD_BALANCING.md
!/PHASE9_OBSERVABILITY.md
!/PHASE10_FAILURE_HANDLING.md
!/PHASE11_AWS.md
!/PHASE12_DOCKER.md
!/PHASE13_CICD.md

# NOT re-admitted, pending an explicit decision (see README):
#   PHASE0_DOMAIN_ANALYSIS.md  -- analyses the legacy system
#   ARCHITECTURE.md            -- pre-existing, describes the legacy system
#   dbmigaratiom.md            -- pre-existing legacy notes
#   prompt.md                  -- personal brief, not project code
